 **Artifacts:** `apps/platform-api/scripts/capture-check.mjs` (reusable precondition check — re-run after
 capture lands to confirm the store is non-empty before resuming).
+
+## 2026-07-24 · Diagnosis (why the store is empty) — ROOT CAUSE = reflection has no trigger (3ecc1859)
+
+Extended the capture check to the related tables. The store isn't empty because nothing is captured —
+it's empty because the **reflection step never runs**:
+
+| Table | Rows | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `proposals` | 4, **all `status='applied'`** | Agent proposals were created AND accepted (`decided_at` set) |
+| `proposals.reflected_at` | **null on all 4** | Reflection never distilled the applied proposals into memories |
+| `memories` | 0 | (consequence) |
+| `run_memory_attributions` | 0 | (consequence — nothing ever injected) |
+
+**Chain:** propose → apply (WORKS) → **reflect applied proposals → memories (NEVER RUNS)** → 0 memories →
+ranker moot. `runReflection` is reachable only via `POST /api/agent/reflection`; no cron/scheduler/event
+invokes it (issue **3ecc1859**). The #132 accept path and the Review Inbox are NOT the problem — proposals
+are decided within ~2s.
+
+**Root cause = 3ecc1859 (reflection autonomous trigger).** That is the true unblock for both capture AND
+(downstream) this ranking issue. A cheap validation exists: manually invoking reflection on the 4 applied
+proposals should produce memories (confirms the engine works and the ONLY gap is the trigger) — but that
+WRITES to prod `memories`, so it needs explicit go-ahead.
